# Privacy Policy

## Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect through the Clinical Intelligence application and browser extension, how we use it, and how we protect it.

Clinical Intelligence is a service designed to support healthcare professionals with clinical workflows and patient communication.

The information we collect is used to provide and improve the service. We do not sell personal information or use it for advertising.

## Information Collection and Use

To provide the service, we may collect information including:

* Patient name
* Phone number
* Date of birth
* Gender
* Medical and clinical information
* Information provided during patient communication

This information is used to provide the functionality of the Clinical Intelligence service and related communication features.

## Chrome Extension and EHR Data

The Clinical Intelligence EHR Capture browser extension allows healthcare professionals to capture relevant information from an EHR page for use within the Clinical Intelligence service.

The extension accesses the active EHR page only when the clinician explicitly initiates a capture. The clinician remains in control of when information is captured. The extension does not continuously monitor EHR pages or automatically capture information in the background.

Captured information may include patient details and clinical information displayed on the EHR page. Captured information is securely transmitted to the Clinical Intelligence service for processing and to provide the requested functionality.

The captured information is not sold or used for advertising.

## Communication

The Clinical Intelligence service may use third-party communication services, including the WhatsApp Cloud API, to communicate with patients as part of the service.

Information provided through these communications may be processed and stored by Clinical Intelligence to provide the service.

## Data Storage

Personal and medical data is securely stored using Supabase database infrastructure. We take appropriate security measures to protect data against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.

## Service Providers

We may use third-party companies and individuals to:

* Provide and maintain the service
* Process and store data
* Support application functionality
* Provide communication services
* Monitor system performance

These providers process information on our behalf and are required to protect the information and use it only for purposes related to providing their services.

## Security

We use commercially reasonable measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.

However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page and take effect upon posting.

